claimed: script-cli-spec -- operator ask 2026-09-07: a CLI for okay-script, serve among its verbs but not the point of it -- running documents, generating content, the mdoc-style check. Spec section in specs/okay-script.md plus BACKLOG: `okay script serve|run|render|build|check|new`, sharing the `okay` binary the deployment CLI introduces. `build` is the static-site half the container never had (render every page once to files, no server, nothing to keep alive), `check` is the mdoc-style gate that answers the sbt-test integration question DECLINED earlier in a better form (a command CI runs, not a task inside the build), and `run` is ScalaScript.run for a document that is a program. Spec only.
